group: D3h
formula: BF3
construction: a central atom and its neighbours
headline: 
note: Fragments: a central atom and its neighbours · energies in Hartree · simplified (Show all levels draws everything) · labels in D<sub>3h</sub> · 4 core orbitals hidden
about: **What is drawn.** The molecular levels in the middle are the calculation's own orbital energies, in Hartree.\n\n**Fragment levels.** Each fragment level is placed at the mean of the molecular orbitals it became, weighted by its share of them, and kept in the atom's own shell order. Its free-atom energy is given beside it.\n\n**Simplified.** Lines to non-bonding levels are not drawn; the ligands' non-bonding levels are one grey block. Tick Show all levels to draw everything.\n\n**Symmetry.** Symmetry labels computed from the orbitals in D3h; the code reported none.\n\n**The circles beside each symmetry orbital** show the atoms as seen from one side, filled and open for opposite sign and sized by weight; a bar is a p lobe in the page.\n\n**Not shown.** 4 core orbitals below −6.68 Hartree.
